# Security

Short version: this project has no secrets, holds no value, and cannot move
funds on its own.

## No private keys, ever

This project does not generate, create, request, import, derive, read, store or
transmit a private key, a seed phrase, or a keystore. Not in the default
scaffold, not in the consent-gated modules, not in any code path at all. There
is no key file to configure, and adding one would be a design error.

If any code in this project ever asks you for a private key or a recovery
phrase, it is not this project.

## You sign in your own wallet

A withdrawal intent is unsigned data: a description, plus a hash of that
description, plus an expiry. It is not a transaction, not an authorisation and
not a transfer.

Producing anything of effect from an intent happens in your own wallet
software, outside this application, on your own hardware, at a moment you chose.
This application can show you the intent; it cannot sign it for you and it
cannot send it for you.

## Nothing is automatic

There is no scheduler, no timer, no retry loop, no queue worker, no batch job and
no reconnect-and-resend behaviour anywhere in this project. Every chain call in
the default scaffold is a read.

The two consent-gated modules (`src/wallet/signing.ts` and
`src/wallet/broadcast.ts`) are not written to disk by a normal
`melodie init --template {{TEMPLATE}}` run. They exist only if an operator
explicitly asked for them at generation time, and even then every entry point
requires an operator-supplied consent token, and every send additionally
requires a human confirmation callback that must return exactly `true`.

## Chain scope

Only testnets are configured. Mainnet is not in the configuration table at all.
The default chain is Sepolia, and the application refuses to start if the
default chain is ever changed to a mainnet.

## Do not paste keys into issues

If you open a security issue:

- **do not** paste a private key, a seed phrase, a `.env` file with a populated
  `RPC_URL`, an API key, or a JWT;
- redact anything that looks like a credential before you paste it;
- prefer describing the behaviour over pasting a payload.

A report containing a live credential is a report containing somebody's money.
Scrub it first, and say in the report that you did.

## Reporting a problem

Report security issues privately to the maintainer of this repository. Until a
real address exists, use the repository's private security-advisory channel
rather than opening a public issue, and put `SECURITY CONTACT: TODO` in the
first line so the maintainer knows to rotate the contact.

## What this is not

This is a scaffold. It is not a wallet, not a custodian, not a payments
processor, and not an audited system. No audit has been performed, and no claim
of one should be made on the basis of this file existing.
